{
  "title": "56: al-Waaqeah الواقعة",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِذَا وَقَعَتِ الْوَاقِعَةُ ۙ‏(1)\nEZAA WAQA-A’TIL WAAQE-A’TO.\nWhen the Imminent [Hour] befalls\nلَيْسَ لِوَقْعَتِهَا كَاذِبَةٌ ۘ‏(2)\nLAYSA LE-WAQA’TEHAA KAAZEBAH.\n—there is no denying that it will befall—\nخَافِضَةٌ رَّافِعَةٌ ۙ‏(3)\nKHAAFEZATUR RAAFE-A’TUN.\n[it will be] lowering and exalting.\nاِذَا رُجَّتِ الْاَرْضُ رَجًّا ۙ‏(4)\nEZAA RUJJATIL ARZO RAJJANW.\nWhen the earth is shaken violently,\nوَّبُسَّتِ الْجِبَالُ بَسًّا ۙ‏(5)\nWA BUSSATIL JEBAALO BASSAN.\nand the mountains are shattered into bits\nفَكَانَتْ هَبَآءً مُّنْۢبَثًّا ۙ‏(6)\nFA-KAANAT HABAAA-AM MUMBASSANW.\nand become scattered dust,\nوَّكُنْتُمْ اَزْوَاجًا ثَلٰثَةً ؕ‏(7)\nWA KUNTUM AZWAAJAN SALAASAH.\nyou will be three groups:\nفَاَصْحٰبُ الْمَيْمَنَةِ ۙ مَاۤ اَصْحٰبُ الْمَيْمَنَةِ ؕ‏(8)\nFA-ASHAABUL MAYMANATE MAA ASHAABUL MAYMANAH.\nThe People of the Right Hand—and what are the People of the Right Hand?!\nوَاَصْحٰبُ الْمَشْئَمَةِ ۙ مَاۤ اَصْحٰبُ الْمَشْئَمَةِؕ‏(9)\nWA ASHAABUL MASH-AMATE, MAA ASHAABUL MASH-AMAH.\nAnd the People of the Left Hand—and what are the People of the Left Hand?!\nوَالسّٰبِقُوْنَ السّٰبِقُوْنَۚ  ۙ‏(10)\nWAS-SAABEQOONAS SAABEQOON.\nAnd the Foremost Ones are the foremost ones:\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَۚ‏(11)\nOOLAAEKAL MOQARRABOON.\nthey are the ones brought near [to Allah],\nفِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِ‏(12)\nFEE JANNATIN NA-EE’M.\n[who will reside] in the gardens of bliss.\nثُلَّةٌ مِّنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(13)\nSULLATUM MENAL AWWALEEN.\nA multitude from the former [generations]\nوَقَلِيْلٌ مِّنَ الْاٰخِرِيْنَؕ‏(14)\nWA QALEELUM MENAL AAKHEREEN.\nand a few from the latter ones.\nعَلٰى سُرُرٍ مَّوْضُوْنَةٍۙ‏(15)\nA’LAA SORORIM MAWZOONATIM.\nOn brocaded couches\nمُّتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلَيْهَا مُتَقٰبِلِيْنَ‏(16)\nMUTTAKE-EENA A’LAYHAA MOTAQAABELEEN.\nreclining on them, face to face.\nيَطُوْفُ عَلَيْهِمْ وِلْدَانٌ مُّخَلَّدُوْنَۙ‏(17)\nYATOOFO A’LAYHIM WILDAANUM MOKHALLADOON.\nThey will be waited upon by immortal youths,\nبِاَكْوَابٍ وَّاَبَارِيْقَ ۙ وَكَاْسٍ مِّنْ مَّعِيْنٍۙ‏(18)\nBE-AKWAABIWN WA ABAAREEQA, WA KAASIM MIM MA-E’ENIL.\nwith goblets and ewers and a cup of a clear wine,\nلَّا يُصَدَّعُوْنَ عَنْهَا وَلَا يُنْزِفُوْنَۙ‏(19)\nLAA YOSADDA-O’ONA A’NHAA WA LAA YUNZEFOON.\nwhich causes them neither headache nor stupefaction,\nوَفَاكِهَةٍ مِّمَّا يَتَخَيَّرُوْنَۙ‏(20)\nWA FAAKEHATIM MIMMAA YATAKHAY-YAROON.\nand such fruits as they prefer\nوَلَحْمِ طَيْرٍ مِّمَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَؕ‏(21)\nWA LAHME TAYRIM MIMMAA YASHTAHOON.\nand such flesh of fowls as they desire,\nوَحُوْرٌ عِيْنٌۙ‏(22)\nWA HOORUN E’ENUN.\nand big-eyed houris\nكَاَمْثَالِ اللُّؤْلُؤِالْمَكْنُوْنِۚ‏(23)\nKA-AMSAALIL LO-LO-IL MAKNOON.\nlike guarded pearls,\nجَزَآءًۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(24)\nJAZAAA-AM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\na reward for what they used to do.\nلَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا لَغْوًا وَّلَا تَاْثِيْمًا ۙ‏(25)\nLAA YASMA-O’ONA FEEHAA LAGHWANW WA LAA TAA-SEEMAN.\nThey will not hear therein any vain talk or sinful speech,\nاِلَّا قِيْلًا سَلٰمًا سَلٰمًا‏(26)\nILLAA QEELAN SALAAMAN SALAAMAA.\nbut only the watchword, ‘Peace!’ ‘Peace!’\nوَاَصْحٰبُ الْيَمِيْنِ ۙ مَاۤ اَصْحٰبُ الْيَمِيْنِؕ‏(27)\nWA AS-HAABUL YAMEENE, MAA AS-HAABUL YAAMEEN.\nAnd the People of the Right Hand—what are the People of the Right Hand?!\nفِىْ سِدْرٍ مَّخْضُوْدٍۙ‏(28)\nFEE SIDRIM MAKHZOODIN.\nAmid thornless lote trees\nوَّطَلْحٍ مَّنْضُوْدٍۙ‏(29)\nWA TALHIM MANZOODIN.\nand clustered spathes\nوَّظِلٍّ مَّمْدُوْدٍۙ‏(30)\nWA ZILLIM MAMDOODIN.\nand extended shade,\nوَّ مَآءٍ مَّسْكُوْبٍۙ‏(31)\nWA MAAA-IM MASKOOBINW.\nand ever-flowing water\nوَّفَاكِهَةٍ كَثِيْرَةٍۙ‏(32)\nWA FAAKEHATIN KASEERATIL.\nand abundant fruits,\nلَّا مَقْطُوْعَةٍ وَّلَا مَمْنُوْعَةٍۙ‏(33)\nLAA MAQTOO-A’TIN WA LAA MAMNOO-A’TINW.\nneither inaccessible, nor forbidden,\nوَّ فُرُشٍ مَّرْفُوْعَةٍؕ‏(34)\nWA FOROSHIM MARFOO-A’H.\nand noble spouses.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْشَاْنٰهُنَّ اِنْشَآءًۙ‏(35)\nINNAA AN-SHAANAAHUNNA INSHAA-AN.\nWe have created them with a special creation,\nفَجَعَلْنٰهُنَّ اَبْكَارًاۙ‏(36)\nFA JA-A’LNAAHUNNA ABKAARAN.\nand made them virgins,\nعُرُبًا اَتْرَابًاۙ‏(37)\nO’ROBAN ATRAABAL.\nloving, of a like age,\nلِّاَصْحٰبِ الْيَمِيْنِؕ‏(38)\nLE-ASHAABIL YAMEEN.\nfor the People of the Right Hand.\nثُلَّةٌ مِّنَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(39)\nSULLATUM MENAL AWWALEENA.\nA multitude from the former [generations]\nوَثُلَّةٌ مِّنَ الْاٰخِرِيْنَؕ‏(40)\nWA SULLATUM MENAL AAKHEREEN.\nand a multitude from the latter [ones].\nوَاَصْحٰبُ الشِّمَالِ ۙ مَاۤ اَصْحٰبُ الشِّمَالِؕ‏(41)\nWA AS-HAABUSH SHEMAALE, MAA AS-HAABUSH SHEMAAL.\nAnd the People of the Left Hand—what are the People of the Left Hand?!\nفِىْ سَمُوْمٍ وَّحَمِيْمٍۙ‏(42)\nFEE SAMOOMINW WA HAMEEMIWNW.\nAmid infernal miasma and boiling water\nوَّظِلٍّ مِّنْ يَّحْمُوْمٍۙ‏(43)\nWA ZILLIM MINY YAHMOOMIL.\nand the shadow of a dense black smoke,\nلَّا بَارِدٍ وَّلَا كَرِيْمٍ‏(44)\nLAA BAAREDINW WA LAA KAREEM.\nneither cool nor beneficial.\nاِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَبْلَ ذٰ لِكَ مُتْرَفِيْنَۚ  ۖ‏(45)\nINNAHUM KAANOO QABLA ZAALEKA MUTRAFEEN.\nIndeed they had been affluent before this,\nوَكَانُوْا يُصِرُّوْنَ عَلَى الْحِنْثِ الْعَظِيْمِۚ‏(46)\nWA KAANOO YOSIRROONA A’LAL HINSIL A’ZEEM.\nand they used to persist in the great sin.\nوَكَانُوْا يَقُوْلُوْنَ ۙ اَئِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَۙ‏(47)\nWA KAANU YAQOOLOONA, A-EZAA MITNAA WA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MABO’OSOON.\nAnd they used to say, ‘What! When we are dead and become dust and bones, shall we be resurrected?!\nاَوَاٰبَآؤُنَا الْاَوَّلُوْنَ‏(48)\nAWA-AABAAA-ONAL AWWALOON.\nAnd our forefathers too?!’\nقُلْ اِنَّ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(49)\nQUL INNAL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHEREEN.\nSay, ‘Indeed the former and latter generations\nلَمَجْمُوْعُوْنَ ۙ اِلٰى مِيْقَاتِ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍ‏(50)\nLA-MAJMOO-OO’NA, ELAA MEEQAATE YAWMIM MA’LOOM.\nwill all be gathered for the tryst of a known day.\nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ اَيُّهَا الضَّآلُّوْنَ الْمُكَذِّبُوْنَۙ‏(51)\nSUMMA INNAKUM AYYOHAZ ZAALLOONAL MOKAZZEBOON.\nThen indeed, you, astray deniers,\nلَاٰكِلُوْنَ مِنْ شَجَرٍ مِّنْ زَقُّوْمٍۙ‏(52)\nLA-AAKELOONA MIN SHAZARIM MIN ZAQQOOMIN.\nwill surely eat from the Zaqqum tree\nفَمٰلِئُوْنَ مِنْهَا الْبُطُوْنَۚ‏(53)\nFAMAA-LE-OONA MINHAL BOTOON.\nand stuff your bellies with it,\nفَشٰرِبُوْنَ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الْحَمِيْمِۚ‏(54)\nFA-SHAAREBOONA A’LAYHE MENAL HAMEEM.\nand drink boiling water on top of it,\nفَشٰرِبُوْنَ شُرْبَ الْهِيْمِؕ‏(55)\nFA-SHAAREBOONA SHURBAL HEEM.\ndrinking like thirsty camels.’\nهٰذَا نُزُلُهُمْ يَوْمَ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(56)\nHAAZAA NOZOLOHUM YAWMAD DEEN.\nSuch will be the hospitality they receive on the Day of Retribution.\nنَحْنُ خَلَقْنٰكُمْ فَلَوْلَا تُصَدِّقُوْنَ‏(57)\nNAHNO KHALAQNAAKUM FA-LAWLAA TOSADDEQOON.\nWe created you. Then why do you not acknowledge it?\nاَفَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا تُمْنُوْنَؕ‏(58)\nAFA-RA-AYTUM MAA TUMNOON.\nHave you considered the sperm that you emit?\nءَاَنْتُمْ تَخْلُقُوْنَهٗۤ اَمْ نَحْنُ الْخٰلِقُوْنَ‏(59)\nA-ANTUM TAKHLOQOO-NAHU AM NAHNUL KHAALEQOON.\nIs it you who create it, or are We the creator?\nنَحْنُ قَدَّرْنَا بَيْنَكُمُ الْمَوْتَ وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَسْبُوْقِيْنَۙ‏(60)\nNAHNO QADDARNAA BAYNAKOMUL MAWTA WA MAA NAHNO BE-MASBOOQEEN.\nWe have ordained death among you, and We are not to be outmaneuvered\nعَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّبَدِّلَ اَمْثَالَكُمْ وَنُنْشِئَكُمْ فِىْ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(61)\nA’LAA AN NOBADDELA AMSAALAKUM WA NUNSHE-AKUM FEE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nfrom replacing you with your likes and recreating you in [a realm] you do not know.\nوَلَقَدْ عَلِمْتُمُ النَّشْاَةَ الْاُوْلٰى فَلَوْلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA LAQAD A’LIMTOMUN NASH-ATAL OOLAA FA LAWLAA TAZAKKAROON.\nCertainly you have known the first genesis, then why do you not take admonition?\nاَفَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا تَحْرُثُوْنَؕ‏(63)\nAFARA-AYTUM MAA TAHROSOON.\nHave you considered what you sow?\nءَاَنْتُمْ تَزْرَعُوْنَهٗۤ اَمْ نَحْنُ الزّٰرِعُوْنَ‏(64)\nA-ANTUM TAZRA-O’ONAHU AM NAHNUZ ZAARE-O’ON.\nIs it you who make it grow, or are We the grower?\nلَوْ نَشَآءُ لَجَعَلْنٰهُ حُطَامًا فَظَلْتُمْ تَفَكَّهُوْنَ‏(65)\nLAW NASHAAA-O LAJA-A’LNAAHO HOTAAMAN FA ZALTUM TAFAKKAHOON.\nIf We wish, We turn it into chaff, whereat you are left stunned [saying to yourselves,]\nاِنَّا لَمُغْرَمُوْنَۙ‏(66)\nINNAA LA MUGHRAMOON.\n‘Indeed we have suffered loss!\nبَلْ نَحْنُ مَحْرُوْمُوْنَ‏(67)\nBAL NAHNO MAHROOMOON.\nNo, we are deprived!’\nاَفَرَءَيْتُمُ الْمَآءَ الَّذِىْ تَشْرَبُوْنَؕ‏(68)\nAFARA-AYTOMUL MAAA-AL LAZEE TASHRABOON.\nHave you considered the water that you drink?\nءَاَنْتُمْ اَنْزَلْتُمُوْهُ مِنَ الْمُزْنِ اَمْ نَحْنُ الْمُنْزِلُوْنَ‏(69)\nA-ANTUM ANZALTOMOOHO MENAL MUZNE AM NAHNUL MUNZELOON.\nIs it you who bring it down from the rain cloud, or is it We who bring [it] down?\nلَوْ نَشَآءُ جَعَلْنٰهُ اُجَاجًا فَلَوْلَا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(70)\nLAW NASHAAA-O JA-A’LNAAHO OJAAJAN FALAWLAA TASHKOROON.\nIf We wish We can make it bitter. Then why do you not give thanks?\nاَفَرَءَيْتُمُ النَّارَ الَّتِىْ تُوْرُوْنَؕ‏(71)\nAFARA-AYTOMUN NAARAL LATEE TOOROON.\nHave you considered the fire that you kindle?\nءَاَنْتُمْ اَنْشَاْتُمْ شَجَرَتَهَاۤ اَمْ نَحْنُ الْمُنْشِئُوْنَ‏(72)\nA-ANTUM AN-SHAATUM SHAJARATAHAA AM NAHNUL MUNSHE-OON.\nWas it you who caused its tree to grow, or were We the grower?\nنَحْنُ جَعَلْنٰهَا تَذْكِرَةً وَّمَتَاعًا لِّلْمُقْوِيْنَۚ‏(73)\nNAHNO JA-A’LNAAHAA TAZKERATANW WA MATAA-A’L LILMUQWEEN.\nIt was We who made it a reminder and a boon for the desert-dwellers.\nفَسَبِّحْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(74)\nFA-SABBEH BISME RABBEKAL A’ZEEM.\nSo celebrate the Name of your Lord, the All-supreme.\nفَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِمَوٰقِعِ النُّجُوْمِۙ‏‏(75)\nFALAA UQSEMO BE MAWAA-QE-I’N NOJOOM.\nI swear by the places where the stars set!\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَقَسَمٌ لَّوْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ عَظِيْمٌۙ‏(76)\nWA INNAHU LAQASAMUL LAW TA’LAMOONA A’ZEEM.\nAnd indeed it is a great oath, should you know.\nاِنَّهٗ لَقُرْاٰنٌ كَرِيْمٌۙ‏(77)\nINNAHU LA-QURAANUN KAREEMUN.\nThis is indeed a noble Quran,\nفِىْ كِتٰبٍ مَّكْنُوْنٍۙ‏(78)\nFEE KETAABIM MAKNOONIL.\nin a guarded Book\nلَّا يَمَسُّهٗۤ اِلَّا الْمُطَهَّرُوْنَؕ‏(79)\nLAA YAMASSOHU ILLAL MOTAHHAROON.\n—no one touches it except the pure ones—\nتَنْزِيْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(80)\nTANZEELUM MIR RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nsent down gradually from the Lord of all the worlds.\nاَفَبِهٰذَا الْحَدِيْثِ اَنْتُمْ مُّدْهِنُوْنَۙ‏(81)\nAFA-BE HAAZAL HADEESE ANTUM MUDHENOON.\nWhat! Do you take lightly this discourse?\nوَتَجْعَلُوْنَ رِزْقَكُمْ اَنَّكُمْ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(82)\nWA TAJ-A’LOONA RIZQAKUM ANNAKUM TOKAZZEBOON.\nAnd make your denial of it your vocation?\nفَلَوْلَاۤ اِذَا بَلَغَتِ الْحُلْقُوْمَۙ‏(83)\nFALAWLAA EZAA BALAGHATIL HULQOOM.\nSo when it reaches the throat [of the dying person],\nوَاَنْتُمْ حِيْنَئِذٍ تَنْظُرُوْنَۙ‏(84)\nWA ANTUM HEENA-EZIN TANZOROON.\nand at that moment you are looking on [at his bedside]\nوَنَحْنُ اَقْرَبُ اِلَيْهِ مِنْكُمْ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA NAHNO AQRABO ELAYHE MINKUM WA LAAKIL LAA TUBSEROON.\n—and We are nearer to him than you are, though you do not perceive—\nفَلَوْلَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ غَيْرَ مَدِيْنِيْنَۙ‏(86)\nFA-LAWLAA IN KUNTUM GHAYRA MADEENEEN.\nthen why do you not restore it, if you are not subject\nتَرْجِعُوْنَهَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(87)\nTARJE-O’ONAHAA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\n[to Divine dispensation], if you are truthful?\nفَاَمَّاۤ اِنْ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَۙ‏(88)\nFA-AMMAA IN KAANA MENAL MOQARRABEEN.\nThen, if he be of those brought near,\nفَرَوْحٌ وَّ رَيْحَانٌ ۙ وَّجَنَّتُ نَعِيْمٍ‏(89)\nFA RAWHUNW WA RAYHAANUNW, WA JANNATO NA-EE’M.\nthen ease, abundance, and a garden of bliss.\nوَاَمَّاۤ اِنْ كَانَ مِنْ اَصْحٰبِ الْيَمِيْنِۙ‏(90)\nWA AMMAA IN KAANA MIN ASHAABIL YAMEEN.\nAnd if he be of the People of the Right Hand,\nفَسَلٰمٌ لَّكَ مِنْ اَصْحٰبِ الْيَمِيْنِؕ‏(91)\nFA-SALAAMUL LAKA MIN AS-HAABIL YAMEEN.\nthen [he will be told,] ‘Peace be on you, from the People of the Right Hand!’\nوَاَمَّاۤ اِنْ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ الضَّآلِّيْنَۙ‏(92)\nWA AMMAA IN KAANA MENAL MOKAZZEBEENAZ ZAAL-LEEN.\nBut if he be of the impugners, the astray ones,\nفَنُزُلٌ مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍۙ‏(93)\nFANOZOLUM MIN HAMEEMINW.\nthen a treat of boiling water\nوَّتَصْلِيَةُ جَحِيْمٍ‏(94)\nWA TASLEYATO JAHEEM.\nand entry into hell.\nاِنَّ هٰذَا لَهُوَ حَقُّ الْيَقِيْنِۚ‏(95)\nINNA HAAZAA LAHOWA HAQQUL YAQEEN.\nIndeed this is certain truth.\nفَسَبِّحْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(96)\nFA-SABBEH BISME RABBEKAL A’ZEEM.\nSo celebrate the Name of your Lord, the All-supreme!",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 96 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that a person who recites this Surah will not be from among the absent-minded ones. Poverty does not come near this person.\nImam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) said that the one who recites Surah al-Waqea’h will have a shining face of the Day of Reckoning. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah on every Friday, will be from those whom Allah (s.w.t.) loves and he will be loved by people also. He will be free from troubles and poverty and will be counted from the loyal companions of Imam Ali (a.s.). Reciting this Surah on a dead person leads to all his sins being forgiven and if the person is on his deathbed then he will die with ease.\nKeeping this Surah in one’s possession is a means of increase in sustenance. Imam Ali Zainul Abideen (a.s.) has narrated that if a person recites this Surah (at night) on the first night of the lunar month and then continues to recite the same Surah, increasing the number of times to coincide with the date, such that on the tenth night he recites it ten times, until the fourteenth night, then his sustenance will increase greatly."
